{"id":"claim:complex/lexical-head-formal-noun-nominalization--siri-way-of-action-after-verb","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/lexical-head-formal-noun-nominalization","topics":["topic:complex/lexical-head-formal-noun-nominalization","topic:complex/lexical-head-formal-noun-nominalization--division-of-labour"],"statement":{"en":"The nominalizer siri may be used after action verbs to mean the 'way of action' when followed by a descriptive expression.","ja":"名詞化辞siriは動作動詞の後に用いられて記述的表現を伴うとき、「動作の仕方」を意味することがある。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"existential","modality":"descriptive","conditions":["followed by a descriptive expression"]},"forms":["siri"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0257-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-31-28-856Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/lexical-head-formal-noun-nominalization--pokon-kotom-appearance-not-reality","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/lexical-head-formal-noun-nominalization","topics":["topic:complex/lexical-head-formal-noun-nominalization","topic:complex/lexical-head-formal-noun-nominalization--lexicalized"],"statement":{"en":"The nominalizers pokon and kotom indicate that the preceding verb describes how things appear to the speaker, not necessarily how they really are.","ja":"名詞化辞pokonとkotomは、前接する動詞が話し手にとってどのように見えるかを表し、必ずしも実際の状態とは限らないことを示す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"descriptive","conditions":[]},"forms":["pokon","kotom"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0257-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:complex/lexical-head-formal-noun-nominalization--pokon-pretence-appearance","differs_in":"scope","note":"The pokon-pretence claim narrows the appearance semantics to the specific sub-case of agent pretence for pokon alone."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-31-28-856Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/lexical-head-formal-noun-nominalization--pokon-pretence-appearance","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/lexical-head-formal-noun-nominalization","topics":["topic:complex/lexical-head-formal-noun-nominalization","topic:complex/lexical-head-formal-noun-nominalization--lexicalized"],"statement":{"en":"The nominalizer pokon often indicates that the appearance of things is due to pretence on the part of the agent.","ja":"名詞化辞pokonは、その外見が動作主側の見せかけによるものであることをしばしば示す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"frequentative","modality":"descriptive","conditions":[]},"forms":["pokon"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0257-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-31-28-856Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/lexical-head-formal-noun-nominalization--kotom-ruwe-hawe-hita-classified-nominalizers","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/lexical-head-formal-noun-nominalization","topics":["topic:complex/lexical-head-formal-noun-nominalization","topic:complex/lexical-head-formal-noun-nominalization--overview"],"statement":{"en":"Morphemes such as kotom, ruwe, hawe, and hita are classified as nominalizers.","ja":"kotom、ruwe、hawe、hita などの形態素は名詞化辞（nominalizer）に分類される。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"existential","modality":"descriptive","conditions":[]},"forms":["kotom","ruwe","hawe","hita"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0028-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"contrasts","claim":"claim:complex/lexical-head-formal-noun-nominalization--concrete-nominalizers-inventory","differs_in":"framework","note":"Statement 4 classifies kotom/ruwe/hawe/hita as nominalizers under a broad ainu scope, while statements 5/7 classify kur/utar/pe/usi/uske/hita as 'concrete' nominalizers in Shizunai dialect, reflecting"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-31-28-856Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/lexical-head-formal-noun-nominalization--concrete-nominalizers-inventory","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/lexical-head-formal-noun-nominalization","topics":["topic:complex/lexical-head-formal-noun-nominalization","topic:complex/lexical-head-formal-noun-nominalization--overview"],"statement":{"en":"Nominalizers of a more concrete nature include kur 'the person who', plural utar 'the people who', pe 'the thing which', usi/uske 'the place where', and hita 'the time when'.","ja":"より具体的な性質を持つ名詞化辞には、kur「〜する人」、その複数形utar「〜する人々」、pe「〜するもの」、usi/uske「〜する場所」、hita「〜する時」がある。"},"type":"membership","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"descriptive","conditions":[]},"forms":["kur","utar","pe","usi","uske","hita"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0258-02","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0259-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:complex/lexical-head-formal-noun-nominalization--concrete-nominalizers-adnominal-demonstrative","differs_in":"scope","note":"The adnominal-demonstrative claim specifies a distributional property of the same set (minus hita), refining the membership claim."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-31-28-856Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/lexical-head-formal-noun-nominalization--concrete-nominalizers-adnominal-demonstrative","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/lexical-head-formal-noun-nominalization","topics":["topic:complex/lexical-head-formal-noun-nominalization","topic:complex/lexical-head-formal-noun-nominalization--overview"],"statement":{"en":"The nominalizers kur, utar, pe, and usi/uske are more noun-like than other nominalizers in that they can also be modified by adnominal demonstratives.","ja":"名詞化辞kur、utar、pe、usi/uskeは連体指示詞によっても修飾されうる点で、他の名詞化辞よりもやや名詞に近い性質を持つ。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"descriptive","conditions":[]},"forms":["kur","utar","pe","usi","uske"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0258-03","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0259-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-31-28-856Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/lexical-head-formal-noun-nominalization--humi-katu-classified-nominalizers","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/lexical-head-formal-noun-nominalization","topics":["topic:complex/lexical-head-formal-noun-nominalization","topic:complex/lexical-head-formal-noun-nominalization--sensory-complements"],"statement":{"en":"humi and katu function as nominalizers.","ja":"humi および katu は名詞化辞として機能する。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"descriptive","conditions":[]},"forms":["humi","katu"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0028-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-31-28-856Z","status":"grouped"}
